    {
      "name": "7. Webhooks (Advanced \u2014 Signature Simulation)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Simulate Monnify SUCCESSFUL_TRANSACTION",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"eventType\": \"SUCCESSFUL_TRANSACTION\",\n  \"eventData\": {\n    \"product\": { \"reference\": \"user-{{userId}}\", \"type\": \"RESERVED_ACCOUNT\" },\n    \"transactionReference\": \"MNFY|TEST|{{$timestamp}}\",\n    \"paymentReference\": \"TEST-{{$timestamp}}\",\n    \"amountPaid\": 50000,\n    \"paymentStatus\": \"PAID\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webhooks/monnify",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "webhooks",
                "monnify"
              ]
            },
            "description": "IMPORTANT: this only actually credits a wallet if verifyTransaction() against the REAL Monnify sandbox API also confirms this transactionReference as PAID \u2014 since we independently re-verify every webhook rather than trusting the payload. A fully self-contained Postman-only simulation (without a matching real Monnify sandbox transaction) will correctly be rejected as unverifiable. Use this primarily to test signature verification itself (see pre-request script), not to fabricate a fake credit."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const secretKey = pm.environment.get('monnifySecretKey');",
                  "const body = pm.request.body.raw;",
                  "const hash = CryptoJS.HmacSHA512(body, secretKey).toString(CryptoJS.enc.Hex);",
                  "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'monnify-signature', value: hash });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Simulate Paystack transfer.success",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event\": \"transfer.success\",\n  \"data\": { \"reference\": \"REPLACE_WITH_REAL_WITHDRAWAL_IDEMPOTENCY_KEY\", \"status\": \"success\" }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/webhooks/paystack",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "webhooks",
                "paystack"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Like the Monnify simulation above, this is independently re-verified against the real Paystack /transfer/verify endpoint before anything happens \u2014 this is mainly useful for testing signature verification and the 'unknown reference' handling path, not for fabricating a fake successful withdrawal."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "const secretKey = pm.environment.get('paystackSecretKey');",
                  "const body = pm.request.body.raw;",
                  "const hash = CryptoJS.HmacSHA512(body, secretKey).toString(CryptoJS.enc.Hex);",
                  "pm.request.headers.upsert({ key: 'x-paystack-signature', value: hash });"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
